  "confidence": 0.92,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R62"],
      "pins": ["R62.1", "R62.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R62 has schematic value \"24k\", but its MPN field is \"FRC0805J240TSD\" and its description specifies a 24Ω 0805 resistor. R62 is connected directly between VOUTP and VOUTN, the PoE-derived rails.",
      "expected": "The part used across VOUTP/VOUTN should match the intended high-value PoE signature/bleeder resistance, roughly 24kΩ to 24.9kΩ, not 24Ω. The MPN/description should agree with the 24k value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R62\")\n      (value \"24k\")\n      (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"Description\") \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R62\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R62\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled using the listed 24Ω MPN, the PoE signature resistance is about 1000 times too low. The PSE may fail to detect the board as a valid PD, and if 48V is applied, R62 would dissipate roughly 96W, likely damaging the resistor or the PoE source. If assembled to the 24k value, the BOM/sourcing metadata is still inconsistent.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design is mostly consistent, but R62 has a clear value/sourcing mismatch: its schematic value is 24k while its MPN and description specify 24Ω, and it sits directly across the PoE rails VOUTP/VOUTN. This would likely break PoE detection or cause severe overheating if built per the listed MPN."
}

